=== Prompt ===
Who is Kratos from God of War?

=== Normal Response ===
Kratos is the main protagonist of the popular video game series 'God of War.' He is a fictional character created by David Jaffe and Stig Asmussen. Kratos is a Greek demigod, the son of Zeus, and a skilled warrior. He is known for his brutal and violent nature, as well as his iconic Blades of Chaos, a pair of large, chain-like blades attached to his arms.

Throughout the series, Kratos is driven by a desire for revenge against the gods of Olympus, particularly Zeus, who killed his family and wife, Lysandra, and his daughter, Calliope. Kratos' backstory is deeply rooted in Greek mythology, and his actions are often influenced by his rage and anger towards the gods.

Kratos first appeared in the 2005 game 'God of War,' which was released for the PlayStation 2. The game was a critical and commercial success, and it spawned a series of sequels, prequels, and spin-offs. The character has undergone significant development throughout the series, evolving from a brutal and vengeful warrior to a more complex and nuanced character.

In 2018, a soft reboot of the series was released, titled 'God of War,' which takes place many years after the events of the previous games. In this new game, Kratos has moved on from his past and is living in the Norse realm of Midgard with his new family, including his son Atreus. This new game received widespread critical acclaim for its storytelling, characters, and gameplay.

Kratos has become an iconic character in the world of gaming, known for his brutal combat style and his complex, often conflicted personality. He has been voiced by actor Terrence C. Carson in the original Greek-era games and by Christopher Judge in the Norse-era games.

