Kratos is the main protagonist of the popular video game series 'God of War' developed by Sony's Santa Monica Studio. He first appeared in the 2005 game 'God of War' and has since become one of the most recognizable and iconic characters in the world of video games.

Kratos is a Spartan warrior who was once a slave to the Olympian god of war, Ares. He was driven by a desire for power and control, but after a series of events, he became the new 'God of War' and later the 'God of War' of the Norse pantheon. Throughout the series, Kratos' character undergoes significant development, from a vengeful and bloodthirsty warrior to a more complex and family-oriented character.

Kratos' past is marked by the death of his family, which was ordered by the gods. This event sets the stage for his quest for revenge against the gods and his eventual rise to power. Throughout the series, he battles against various gods and monsters from both the Greek and Norse mythologies, including Ares, Athena, and Baldur.

The character of Kratos has been voiced by actor Christopher Judge since the first game. He is known for his brutal combat style, which often involves using the Blades of Chaos, a pair of magical chains with blades on the end. Kratos' character design and abilities have been widely influential in the world of video games and have become a symbol of the 'God of War' franchise.

The 2018 soft-reboot of the series, 'God of War' (2018), marked a significant change in the character's story and design. This game, set many years after the events of the previous games, follows an older and more matured Kratos as he travels through the world of Norse mythology with his son Atreus. This game received widespread critical acclaim and won several awards, including several Game of the Year awards.

The character of Kratos has also been featured in other media, including a live-action television series, 'God of War' (2022), which serves as a prequel to the 2018 game. The show stars actor Barney Harris as a younger version of the character. Overall, Kratos remains one of the most recognizable and beloved characters in the world of video games.

